WEBVTT

00:00:00.059 --> 00:00:03.779
The current self-hosted quick start describes a single Linux-server

00:00:03.779 --> 00:00:05.940
evaluation using Docker Compose.

00:00:06.320 --> 00:00:09.720
Plan separate web, API, and events hostnames.

00:00:10.140 --> 00:00:13.000
Infrastructure operation is a separate learning path from

00:00:13.000 --> 00:00:14.420
department administration.

00:00:15.049 --> 00:00:19.490
Review the supported installer, generate deployment-specific credentials, and

00:00:19.490 --> 00:00:21.520
inspect the resulting configuration.

00:00:21.899 --> 00:00:27.159
Start the stack, review worker migration progress, and verify all three endpoints.

00:00:27.530 --> 00:00:30.659
Create the first account and department after initialization.

00:00:31.409 --> 00:00:34.389
Department screens configure operational behavior.

00:00:34.800 --> 00:00:38.220
In this checkout, host configuration uses public static

00:00:38.220 --> 00:00:40.220
fields in configuration classes.

00:00:40.579 --> 00:00:44.159
The configuration processor reads JSON keys or environment

00:00:44.159 --> 00:00:46.159
variables and assigns those fields.

00:00:46.560 --> 00:00:51.800
Use the source and release documentation to identify the exact host setting; avoid

00:00:51.800 --> 00:00:54.160
applying a generic appsettings recipe.

00:00:54.760 --> 00:00:58.079
Before updating, back up the data and configuration and

00:00:58.079 --> 00:01:00.079
retain prior image references.

00:01:00.449 --> 00:01:04.409
A rollback can require restoring the database as well as the application.

00:01:04.789 --> 00:01:09.730
Treat a running evaluation as the start of operations preparation, with monitoring

00:01:09.760 --> 00:01:11.619
and a tested recovery procedure.

00:01:12.419 --> 00:01:15.850
Detailed infrastructure capture needs the chosen deployment layout:

00:01:16.310 --> 00:01:21.700
Linux Compose, Windows, Kubernetes or k3s, or an Incident Command Kit.

00:01:22.280 --> 00:01:26.639
Record the supported release and verify installation, endpoint connectivity,

00:01:26.899 --> 00:01:29.210
backup, and recovery in that environment.

00:01:29.720 --> 00:01:32.230
Use the linked official guides for the matching layout.

